@base = http://localhost:5110
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@carla = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
# IBANs generated by the factory (numbers 1, 2, 3)
@ibanAlice = FR12 3000 1000 0100 0000 0000 100
@ibanBob = FR28 3000 1000 0100 0000 0000 200
@ibanCarla = FR44 3000 1000 0100 0000 0000 300

############ "Account keeping" context ############

### All the accounts (Alice and Bob in EUR, Carla in USD)
GET {{base}}/accounts

### Transfer from Alice (EUR) to Carla (USD): conversion through the anti-corruption layer
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "beneficiaryIban": "{{ibanCarla}}", "amount": 100 }

### Carla received 108.32 USD
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{carla}}

### Withdrawal of 600 €: accepted
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 600 }

### New withdrawal of 600 € on the same day: refused (aggregate invariant: daily limit of 1,000 €)
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 600 }

### Iban value object: wrong check digits → refused
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "beneficiaryIban": "FR77 3000 6000 0112 3456 7890 189", "amount": 10 }

### Money value object: three decimals → refused
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1.234 }

############ "Compliance" context ############

### Large transfer (≥ 10,000 €): "high" alert, the account stays active
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "beneficiaryIban": "{{ibanBob}}", "amount": 12000 }

### Send 3 times in a row: on the 3rd, Compliance suspects structuring and has Bob's account blocked
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{bob}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "beneficiaryIban": "{{ibanAlice}}", "amount": 10 }

### Bob's account is blocked (request coming from the other context, through the open host service)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{bob}}

### Compliance alerts
GET {{base}}/compliance/alerts

### The same account seen by Compliance: a "vigilance file", with no balance nor limit
GET {{base}}/compliance/files/{{bob}}
